import Lesson from '../../layouts/LessonLayout.astro';

const body = `<h1>4.1b — while Loops: Build a Guessing Game</h1>

<div class="activity basic-app">
    <div class="activity-header">
        <span class="activity-label">Basic Application</span>
        <span class="activity-time">~20 min</span>
    </div>

    <div class="section">
        <h3>Build: Guess the Number</h3>
        <p>Yesterday you explored how <code>while</code> loops repeat code until a condition becomes false. Today you'll use that pattern to build the classic number guessing game.</p>
        <p>Create a class called <code>GuessingGame</code>:</p>
        <ol>
            <li>Generate a secret number: <code>int secret = (int)(Math.random() * 100) + 1;</code></li>
            <li>Hardcode a guess (try several values).</li>
            <li>Use a <code>while</code> loop that keeps running <strong>while guess != secret</strong>.</li>
            <li>Inside the loop: print "Too high!" or "Too low!" based on the guess.</li>
            <li>Count how many guesses it took.</li>
        </ol>
    </div>

    <div class="section">
        <h3>Infinite Loop Trap</h3>
        <p>What happens if you forget to update <code>guess</code> inside the loop? Try it (be ready to stop your program). This is the most common while-loop bug. How would you prevent it?</p>
    </div>
</div>

<div class="resources">
    <h3>Reference Docs</h3>
    <ul>
        <li><a href="../docs/unit-04/while-loops.html">Iteration: while &amp; for</a></li>
        <li><a href="../docs/unit-02/math-class.html">Math.random()</a></li>
    </ul>
</div>`;
